{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/210115-your-friendly-fetch","id":210115,"title":"Your Friendly Fetch","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-07-27T07:05:42-07:00","id":210115,"title":"Your Friendly Fetch","content":"Is it possible to ally, and even befriend your fetch? And how are they mechanically different from your average human?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1111-egreham","name":"egreham","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-27T07:16:16-07:00","id":210144,"title":"","content":"Rules for Fetches are in the Changeling core book, with an expanded set of rules in Autumn Nightmares. The big difference is that they have access to Echoes, which let them mirror their Changeling's abilities and do all kinds of cool things with mirrors and shadows. <br /> <br /> As for befriending, absolutely. One of my players was taken by a Fae who liked to punish hypocrites, and when he returned he found that the last twist of the knife was that his Fetch had beeen created to be a a better person than he had ever been. The pair ended up sealing a pledge to aid and protect one another, only slightly complicated by the Fetch's murderous Fetch-spawn of a daughter. They remained firm allies for the entire campaign, and at one point teamed up to kill the player's Keeper.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-27T07:23:19-07:00","id":210167,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/210115-your-friendly-fetch?p=210144#post210144\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for befriending, absolutely. One of my players was taken by a Fae who liked to punish hypocrites, and when he returned he found that the last twist of the knife was that his Fetch had beeen created to be a a better person than he had ever been. The pair ended up sealing a pledge to aid and protect one another, only slightly complicated by the Fetch's murderous Fetch-spawn of a daughter. They remained firm allies for the entire campaign, and at one point teamed up to kill the player's Keeper.</div> </div> </div> </div>... Wait, Fetches can reproduce? I thought they were simple replacement being made of stick and stone and other weird components that's enchanted to look like the replacee.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1111-egreham","name":"egreham","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-27T09:32:13-07:00","id":210295,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>egreham</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/210115-your-friendly-fetch?p=210167#post210167\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ... Wait, Fetches can reproduce?</div> </div> </div> </div>Only if the GM wants them to.<br /> I had a character once who met his Fetch completely by accident after tracking down his mother to a nursing home. The Fetch had some inkling of its own artificial nature, and asserted to my character (a Darkling punk who was taken while living on the street after getting into a fistfight with his father) that he was &quot;a support pillar for a failing system,&quot; and that had the rebellious Changeling not been taken and replaced, the stress he put on his family would have destroyed his parents' marriage and prevented the conception of a sister he was unaware he had.<br /> My character eventually decided that the Fetch was right, and they swore a Good Neighbor's Pact as a mutual &quot;stay out of my way, I'll stay out of yours&quot; agreement.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2709-quatrevingts","name":"QuatreVingts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2709_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"55"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-27T13:29:08-07:00","id":210532,"title":"","content":"There's a changeling in the intro story of Rites of Spring who's taken his fetch as a lover, if I recall correctly.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-27T19:14:48-07:00","id":210704,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Christian A</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/210115-your-friendly-fetch?p=210532#post210532\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's a changeling in the intro story of Rites of Spring who's taken his fetch as a lover, if I recall correctly.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Was his name Narcissus?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1111-egreham","name":"egreham","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-27T21:31:22-07:00","id":210845,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>egreham</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/210115-your-friendly-fetch?p=210167#post210167\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ... Wait, Fetches can reproduce? I thought they were simple replacement being made of stick and stone and other weird components that's enchanted to look like the replacee.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are mechanics for it in Autumn Nightmares. If I remember right, a Fetch who believes it is human and honestly loves its partner can have a child. There can be one of two results, either a child whose blood is poison to the fae or a soulless killer whose very touch destroys glamour and unbinds contracts.<br /> <br /> The one apparent hole in Fetch mechanics are rules for what happens to them when their Changeling hits Wyrd 6+. Because this character allied to his Fetch hit Wyrd 7, and all I could really do for the Fetch was continue to pile on the Echoes (which cap in power at Wyrd 5).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}